     1	# ML6 — ordered limits and contamination control
     2	
     3	**Lane status:** **PROVED-candidate on the D6 separated-packet class;
     4	PARTIAL for unrestricted ML6.**  The positive theorem below uses the PROVED
     5	`S-IDX-MATCH-HS-SEP` norm bridge.  It does not claim that unsmeared (R5)
     6	coefficients have a uniform plane-wave limit, nor that an arbitrary D29
     7	protocol belongs to the separated class.
     8	
     9	## ⟨1⟩1. Theorem ML6-HS-SEP
    10	
    11	**ASSUME.** D6--D8, `J>0`, a fixed hard interval
    12	`I=[a,b]⋐(0,π)`, and a one-sided normalized soft packet
