  1234	## D28 (H-ACE: exact fixed-packet kink--magnon band data)
  1235	  Assume
  1236	H-MQG(1)--(3).  In addition:
  1237	
  1238	1. The kink folium has a covariant positive-energy Hilbert realization
  1239	`(H_{αβ},π_{αβ},U_{αβ})` implementing the commuting infinite-volume time and
  1240	lattice translations.  This is extra structure beyond the state-set
  1241	definition D9/A2.  The vacuum GNS triples are `(H_γ,π_γ,Ω_γ)`, `γ∈{α,β}`
  1242	(D1(d)), with `HΩ_γ=0`; there is no vacuum vector in `H_{αβ}`.
  1243	2. Its Hamiltonian has an isolated finite-multiplicity kink band with
  1244	dispersion `E_K∈C²(𝕋)` (matrix valued on the finite frame index).  A fixed
  1245	Gram-normalized, translation-covariant finite-core ansatz frame gives an
  1246	**exact** band map `Γ_K`, satisfying `H_{αβ}Γ_K=Γ_KE_K`; it is not merely a
  1247	Rayleigh--Ritz approximation.
  1248	3. Each relevant vacuum tail `γ∈{α,β}` has an isolated selected magnon band
  1249	`ω_γ` (identified as `ω` when symmetry relates the tails), gap
  1250	`Δ_M:=min_kω(k)>0`, and Gram-normalized **exact** band map `Γ_{M,γ}`.  A
  1251	spacetime-Schwartz energy-momentum filter of a local observable gives
  1252	almost-local creators `a_{γ,b}(n)` with strictly positive energy transfer and
  1253	with the **momentum-filtered normalisation**
  1254	`a_{γ,b}(n)Ω_γ=Γ_{M,γ}(χ_γe_n⊗e_b)`, `e_n(k):=e^{-ikn}`,
  1255	for a fixed filter `χ_γ∈C_c^∞(𝕋)`; translation covariance makes `χ_γ`
  1256	independent of `n`.  This equality, not merely nonzero overlap with the
  1257	band, is part of the exactness hypothesis.  *(A position-delta normalisation
  1258	— the case `χ_γ≡1` — is not assumed and is in fact incompatible with a
  1259	compactly supported energy--momentum filter.)*
  1260	4. Packet amplitudes are finite sums of `C_c^∞` products and the resulting
  1261	physical packet states lie in the `ℓ¹` class D17.  The dispersions
  1262	are `C^∞` on open neighbourhoods `U_K,U_γ` of their packet momentum supports
  1263	(global `C²` is retained), their kink and magnon velocity supports have
  1264	distance `ε_v>0`, and their signs are: incoming-left `v_M-v_K≥ε_v` at
  1265	`t→-∞`; outgoing-left `v_M-v_K≤-ε_v`; outgoing-right `v_M-v_K≥ε_v` at
  1266	`t→+∞`.  Thus this is a fixed-packet condition and excludes equal velocities
  1267	and the soft endpoint.  **Filter compatibility:** the filters of (3) and the
  1268	kink filter `χ_K∈C_c^∞(𝕋)` satisfy `χ_•≡1` on the corresponding packet
  1269	momentum support and `supp χ_•⊂U_•`; companions `χ̃_•∈C_c^∞(𝕋)` satisfy
  1270	`χ̃_•≡1` on `supp χ_•` and `supp χ̃_•⊂U_•`.  The channel Hamiltonian symbols
  1271	`h_K:=E_Kχ̃_K`, `h_γ:=ω_γχ̃_γ` are then `C^∞(𝕋)` and agree with the
  1272	dispersions on the packet supports.
  1273	5. **(Two-cluster factorization through the vacuum tails.)**  Write
