   178	#### Ordered-limit proof
   179	
   180	**⟨2⟩6.**  For the joint initial dephasing map, the `j`th first moment of
   181	(SG.5) is the initial expectation of `Q̂^{(j)}` minus the jointly dephased
   182	final expectation of `Q̂^{(j)}`.
   183	
   184	*Justification.*  The spectral-expansion computation is exactly
   185	`memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩6 componentwise; item 4 supplies its joint-PVM D27(LR2)
   186	premise.
   187	
   188	**⟨2⟩7.**  After the fixed-window common-sequence limit, item 4 removes the
   189	joint dephasing defect and (SG.4) gives
   190	
   191	\[
   192	 \sum_\nu\nu_jp_W(\nu)
   193	 =-2s_j\,[\omega_W^+(\mathfrak X_W^{(j)})
   194	                -\omega_W^-(\mathfrak X_W^{(j)})].         \tag{SG.6}
   195	\]
   196	
   197	*Justification.*  D27(LR1--LR2), (SG.4), and the scalar proof in claim
   198	M-INDEX-spec (`memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩7.⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2).
   199	
   200	**⟨2⟩8.**  Vector first-moment tightness yields subsequential probabilities
   201	supported on the closed lattice and passes every component first moment to
   202	the limit.  Taking the padded spatial exhaustion in (SG.6) proves (SG.3).
   203	
   204	*Justification.*  Item 4 is D27(LR3) with `‖ν‖_1`, which dominates every
   205	`|ν_j|`; claim M-INDEX-spec supplies the scalar Prokhorov/first-moment step,
   206	and H-MQG(4) fixes the packet and limit order.  **⟨2⟩9. QED.**
   207	
   208	**Scope fence.**  Applying scalar D27 separately proves the `r` marginal
   209	statements of M-INDEX-spec, but it does not by itself prove that the finer
   210	joint dephasing defect vanishes.  The finite joint-lattice conclusion needs
   211	no relaxation assumption; the joint ordered law needs item 4.  Under (S) at
   212	both tails, M-IDX-density additionally gives `2s_j∈ℤ` separately for every
   213	antisymmetric active circle, but that density arithmetic is a conclusion,
   214	not an assumption.
   215	
   216	*Justification.*  D27 is written for one selected scalar charge; claim
   217	M-INDEX-spec explicitly treats D27 as assumed, while claim M-IDX-density
   218	proves the final circlewise density statement under its antisymmetric-tail
   219	hypotheses.
