    14	# SPT-TPM — a channel-free boundary charge-history register
    15	
    16	## 0. Result and exact scope
    17	
    18	The operational edge-memory outcome is the change between two projective
    19	readouts of the **same finite boundary-window charge**.  It is not the spectrum
    20	of the generally noncommuting operator difference and is not D22's existing
    21	wave-operator expression `W_+^†Q_edgeW_+-W_-^†Q_edgeW_-`.
    22	
    23	There are two results.
    24	
    25	1. **`SPT-M'-TPM-fin` (finite theorem).**  Every outcome is an integer before
    26	   any time or window limit.  This uses D19--D20, D26(INT), automorphic
    27	   dynamics, and no relaxation, split, conservation, scattering, or channel
    28	   hypothesis.
    29	2. **`SPT-M'-TPM-spec` (ordered theorem).**  Under the explicitly displayed
    30	   boundary relaxation clauses `(E-LR1)--(E-LR3)`, every ordered limiting law
    31	   is a probability on `ℤ`; its first moment is the ordered change of the
    32	   boundary-window charge.  `(E-LR1)` is supplied by the live PROVED claim
    33	   **LR1-GEN**; the substantive assumptions are `(E-LR2)` and `(E-LR3)`.
    34	
    35	Adding D21(H-split) and the live PROVED claim **SPT-E'** supplies the physical
    36	SPT edge/module interpretation: the registered endpoint is an
    37	`ω_C`-projective module with shifted charge lattice and protected capacity.
    38	Neither input is used to prove TPM support.  In particular this shard does not
    39	identify the full TPM law with the spectral law of D22's channel operator.
    40	
    41	### Exact hypothesis set `(H-SPT-TPM)`
    42	
    43	Fix the following data.
    44	
    45	**(T1) Boundary charge and windows.**  Let `C` be the unbroken D1/D2 tensor and
    46	choose a circle generator `ξ`.  Use D19's boundary profiles
    47	`f_L^{edge}=1_[0,L-1]` and D20's Hermitian, normal-ordered local charge
    48	
    49	`Q_L^∂ := Q^H[f_L^{edge};ξ] = -iQ[f_L^{edge};ξ]`.             **(E.1)**
    50	
    51	`Q_L^∂` is only an abbreviation for the existing D19--D20 object, not a new
    52	definition of charge.
    53	
    54	**(T2) Integral circle.**  D26(INT) holds for the selected normal-ordered
    55	Hermitian one-site charge `S^z_x=-iq_x(ξ)`: for some
    56	`κ∈[0,1)`, `spec S^z_x⊂κ+ℤ`.
    57	
    58	**(T3) Dynamics and preparation.**  The half-chain quasi-local dynamics
    59	`α_t^+` is a strongly continuous one-parameter group of `*`-automorphisms,
    60	and `Ψ` is a unit vector in a representation on which the two measurements are
    61	performed.  D23's AKLT half-chain Hamiltonian is the intended continuous-
    62	symmetry example; more generally one may use any half-chain dynamics meeting
    63	the stated automorphism assumption.  Charge conservation is not needed for
    64	the two theorems below.
    65	
    66	**(T4) Boundary local relaxation `(E-LR)`.**  Let `E_{L,t}` be the spectral
    67	resolution of `Q_L^∂(t):=α_t^+(Q_L^∂)`.  Fix one sequence `T_n→∞` common to
    68	all `L`, and put
    69	
    70	`ω^+_{L,n}(A):=T_n^{-1}∫_[T_n,2T_n]⟨Ψ,α_t^+(A)Ψ⟩dt`,
    71	
    72	`ω^-_{L,n}(A):=T_n^{-1}∫_[-2T_n,-T_n]⟨Ψ,α_t^+(A)Ψ⟩dt`.       **(E.2)**
    73	
    74	For finite `t_-<t_+`, define the escaped-charge and memory-change variables
    75	
    76	`ν:=q_- - q_+`,                 `m:=q_+ - q_-=-ν`,             **(E.3)**
    77	
    78	and the sequential two-projective-measurement law
    79	
    80	`p_{L;t_-,t_+}(ν):=Σ_q ||E_{L,t_+}({q-ν})E_{L,t_-}({q})Ψ||²`. **(E.4)**
    81	
    82	Absent spectral values contribute zero.  The proposed D22 extension
    83	`(E-LR)` consists of:
    84	
    85	- **(E-LR1)** along the same `T_n`, both Cesàro states and every
    86	  double-Cesàro average `p_{L,n}(ν)` of (E.4) converge for every fixed `L`;
    87	- **(E-LR2)** with
    88	  `𝒟_{L,t_-}(A):=Σ_qE_{L,t_-}({q})AE_{L,t_-}({q})`, the
    89	  double-Cesàro average of
    90	  `⟨Ψ,[𝒟_{L,t_-}(Q_L^∂(t_+))-Q_L^∂(t_+)]Ψ⟩` tends to zero for every fixed
    91	  `L` along that same sequence;
    92	- **(E-LR3)** writing `p_L` for the fixed-`L` time limit,
    93	  `lim_{M→∞} sup_L Σ_{|ν|>M}(1+|ν|)p_L(ν)=0`.
    94	
    95	The optional convenience clause is full-sequence weak convergence
    96	`p_L⇒p` as `L→∞`.  Without it all conclusions are per `(E-LR3)` subsequence;
    97	with it the stipulated limit law, hence its first moment, is unique.  The
    98	order is D19's order: infinite-volume dynamics first, fixed-`L` time limits
    99	second, then `L→∞`.
   100	
   101	This is a proposed extension of D22, not a redefinition of live D27.  It is
   102	D27's protocol with `W_m=[a_m,b_m]↑ℤ` replaced by the boundary windows
   103	`[0,L-1]`, and with D13's wall-coordinate ledger replaced by a charge ledger.
   104	
