   107	## 1. Finite boundary-window theorem
   108	
   109	### ⟨1⟩1. THEOREM `SPT-M'-TPM-fin`
   110	
   111	**ASSUME.**  (T1)--(T3), a fixed `L<∞`, and finite times `t_-<t_+`.
   112	
   113	**PROVE.**  There is `κ_L∈ℝ/ℤ` such that
   114	
   115	`spec Q_L^∂(t) ⊂ κ_L+ℤ` for every `t`;                         **(E.5)**
   116	
   117	(E.4) is a probability law; and every escaped-charge outcome `ν` and
   118	edge-memory outcome `m=-ν` lies in `ℤ`.  No commutativity of
   119	`Q_L^∂(t_-)` and `Q_L^∂(t_+)` is assumed.
   120	
   121	**⟨2⟩1 (one-site lattice).**  Every eigenvalue `λ` of the selected Hermitian
   122	one-site charge obeys `λ-κ∈ℤ`.
   123	
   124	*Justification.*  D26(INT); equivalently the finite-dimensional spectral
   125	calculation `e^{2πiλ}=e^{2πiκ}`.  This is donor computation **IDX-FW.1** in
   126	`theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩1.⟨2⟩1 and live claim **M-INDEX-fin**.
   127	
   128	**⟨2⟩2 (boundary-window coset).**  One may take
   129	`κ_L=Lκ (mod ℤ)` in (E.5) at `t=0`.
   130	
   131	*Justification.*  By D19--D20 and (E.1),
   132	`Q_L^∂=Σ_{x=0}^{L-1}S^z_x`.  Different-site terms commute, so finite spectral
   133	addition and ⟨2⟩1 give `spec Q_L^∂⊂Lκ+ℤ`.  This is named arithmetic
   134	**SPT-TPM-FW.1**, the boundary-window instance of donor computation
   135	**IDX-FW.2** and claim **M-INDEX-fin**.
   136	
   137	**⟨2⟩3 (same coset at both times).**  Equation (E.5) holds with that same
   138	`κ_L` for all `t`.
   139	
   140	*Justification.*  Spectrum is invariant under the `C*`-automorphism `α_t^+`
   141	of (T3).  This is named computation **SPT-TPM-FW.2**, identical to donor
   142	**IDX-FW.3** in `theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩1.⟨2⟩4 and claim
   143	**M-INDEX-fin**.
   144	
   145	**⟨2⟩4 (positivity).**  Every weight in (E.4) is nonnegative.
   146	
   147	*Justification.*  It is a sum of squared norms of sequential spectral
   148	projections.  This is donor computation **IDX-TPM.1** in
   149	`theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩5.⟨2⟩1 and claim **M-INDEX-fin**.
   150	
   151	**⟨2⟩5 (normalisation without commutativity).**  Summing over both readouts
   152	gives
   153	
   154	`Σ_{q_-,q_+}||E_{L,t_+}({q_+})E_{L,t_-}({q_-})Ψ||²=||Ψ||²=1`.
   155	
   156	*Justification.*  Apply Parseval first to the final spectral resolution and
   157	then to the initial one; no interchange of projections occurs.  This is
   158	donor computation **IDX-TPM.2** in `theory/memory-index.md`
   159	⟨1⟩5.⟨2⟩2 and live claim **M-INDEX-fin**.
   160	
   161	**⟨2⟩6 (offset cancellation).**  Every nonzero history branch has
   162	`q_-,q_+∈κ_L+ℤ`, whence `ν=q_- -q_+∈ℤ` and `m=-ν∈ℤ`.
   163	
   164	*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩3 and (E.3).  The *same* `L`, profile, normal ordering,
   165	and observable are used in both measurements, so the common `κ_L` cancels
   166	before any limit.  This is named arithmetic **SPT-TPM-FW.3**, identical to
   167	`theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩5.⟨2⟩3 and claim **M-INDEX-fin**; it is not
   168	spectral arithmetic for a difference of noncommuting operators.
   169	
   170	**⟨2⟩7. QED.**
   171	
