   195	## 2. Ordered boundary-memory theorem
   196	
   197	### ⟨1⟩3. LEMMA (finite-window TPM mean)
   198	
   199	**ASSUME.**  The hypotheses of ⟨1⟩1.  Define
   200	`𝒟_{L,t_-}` as in (E-LR2).
   201	
   202	**PROVE.**
   203	
   204	`Σ_ν ν p_{L;t_-,t_+}(ν)
   205	 =⟨Q_L^∂(t_-)⟩-⟨𝒟_{L,t_-}(Q_L^∂(t_+))⟩`.       **(E.6)**
   206	
   207	Equivalently for `r_{L;t_-,t_+}(m):=p_{L;t_-,t_+}(-m)`,
   208	
   209	`Σ_m m r_{L;t_-,t_+}(m)
   210	 =⟨𝒟_{L,t_-}(Q_L^∂(t_+))⟩-⟨Q_L^∂(t_-)⟩`.       **(E.7)**
   211	
   212	**⟨2⟩1.**  Expanding the first measured value gives
   213	`Σ_q q⟨E_{L,t_-}({q})⟩=⟨Q_L^∂(t_-)⟩`.
   214	
   215	*Justification.*  Spectral functional calculus; donor computation
   216	**IDX-TPM.3** in `theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩6 and live claim
   217	**M-INDEX-spec**.
   218	
   219	**⟨2⟩2.**  Expanding the final measured value after the initial projection
   220	gives `⟨𝒟_{L,t_-}(Q_L^∂(t_+))⟩`.
   221	
   222	*Justification.*  Sum over the final spectral resolution inside (E.4), then
   223	use the displayed definition of `𝒟_{L,t_-}`.  This is donor computation
   224	**IDX-TPM.4** in `theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩6 and claim
   225	**M-INDEX-spec**.
   226	
   227	**⟨2⟩3.**  Subtraction proves (E.6), and the change of variable `m=-ν`
   228	proves (E.7).
   229	
   230	*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2 and (E.3); named arithmetic
   231	**SPT-TPM-MEAN.1**.
   232	
   233	**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
   234	
   235	### ⟨1⟩4. THEOREM `SPT-M'-TPM-spec`
   236	
   237	**ASSUME.**  `(H-SPT-TPM)`, including `(E-LR1)--(E-LR3)`.
   238	
   239	**PROVE.**  Every `(E-LR3)`-subsequential ordered limit `p` of the escaped
   240	charge laws is a probability supported on `ℤ`; the reflected edge-memory law
   241	`r(m):=p(-m)` is likewise supported on `ℤ`; and, along that same subsequence,
   242	
   243	`Σ_m m r(m)
   244	 = lim_j[ω^+_{L_j}(Q_{L_j}^∂)-ω^-_{L_j}(Q_{L_j}^∂)]`.          **(E.8)**
   245	
   246	Under the optional full-sequence convergence clause, `p`, `r`, and the value
   247	in (E.8) are unique.
   248	
   249	**⟨2⟩1 (common time subsequence).**  `(E-LR1)` can be satisfied along a
   250	subsequence of every prescribed sequence, simultaneously for all `L`.
   251	
   252	*Justification.*  Live PROVED claim **LR1-GEN** applies because the half-chain
   253	lattice is countable, its quasi-local algebra is separable, `α_t^+` is
   254	strongly continuous by (T3), and every local `Q_L^∂` has finite spectrum by
   255	D19--D20.  LR1-GEN supplies only this binder; it supplies neither (E-LR2) nor
   256	(E-LR3).
   257	
   258	**⟨2⟩2 (remove the dephasing defect).**  At every fixed `L`, double-Cesàro
   259	averaging of (E.6) along the common sequence gives
   260	
   261	`Σ_ννp_L(ν)=ω^-_L(Q_L^∂)-ω^+_L(Q_L^∂)`.                       **(E.9)**
   262	
   263	*Justification.*  (E-LR1) gives the three fixed-window limits and (E-LR2)
   264	sets the averaged difference between the dephased and unmeasured final first
   265	moments to zero.  This is the boundary instance of
   266	`theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩7.⟨2⟩1 and live claim **M-INDEX-spec**.
   267	
   268	**⟨2⟩3 (integer support before exhaustion).**  Each `p_L` is a probability
   269	on `ℤ`.
   270	
   271	*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩1.⟨2⟩4--⟨2⟩6; fixed-`L` convergence in (E-LR1) occurs
   272	on the fixed finite difference set `spec Q_L^∂-spec Q_L^∂⊂ℤ`.  This is also
   273	the fixed-window conclusion of live claims **M-INDEX-fin** and **LR1-GEN**.
   274	
   275	**⟨2⟩4 (spatial compactness and first moments).**  Every subsequence of
   276	`{p_L}` has a further subsequence `p_{L_j}⇒p` for which `p` is a probability
   277	on `ℤ` and `Σ_ννp_{L_j}(ν)→Σ_ννp(ν)`.
   278	
   279	*Justification.*  (E-LR3) is tightness plus uniform integrability of the
   280	first moment.  Prokhorov compactness on the closed set `ℤ` prevents loss of
   281	mass; uniform integrability passes the first moment.  Since every `p_L` is
   282	supported on the closed set `ℤ`, every weak limit is.  This is verbatim the
   283	argument of `theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩7.⟨2⟩3 and live claim
   284	**M-INDEX-spec**, with boundary windows replacing padded two-tail windows.
   285	
   286	**⟨2⟩5 (memory ledger).**  Reflecting by `m=-ν` and taking the same
   287	subsequence in (E.9) gives (E.8).
   288	
   289	*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩2, ⟨2⟩4, and the sign convention (E.3); named
   290	arithmetic **SPT-TPM-MEAN.2**.
   291	
   292	**⟨2⟩6 (no channels hidden in the proof).**  No step introduced wave
   293	operators, asymptotic completeness, bulk/edge channel projections, definite
   294	channel charges, or a scattering matrix.
   295	
   296	*Justification.*  The complete dependency list of leaves ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩5 is
   297	D19--D20, D26, **LR1-GEN**, **M-INDEX-fin**, **M-INDEX-spec**, and the stated
   298	(E-LR2)--(E-LR3) hypotheses.
   299	
   300	**⟨2⟩7. QED.**
