   329	## 3. Exact comparison with the current `SPT-M'`
   330	
   331	The live claim row and `theory/spt-rebuild.md` ⟨1⟩6.⟨2⟩1 currently assume,
   332	in order: `(H-split)`, `(H-AD-edge)`, conservation of the chosen `U(1)`
   333	charge, and asymptotic channels with definite bulk and edge charges.  The
   334	comparison is one line per current hypothesis.
   335	
   336	| current `SPT-M'` hypothesis | role in the current proof | TPM replacement | disposition |
   337	|---|---|---|---|
   338	| D21 `(H-split)` | turns the registered `E_C` edge operator into a physical half-chain edge operator | none for (E.5)--(E.8); retain only when interpreting the protocol in the protected SPT edge module | removed from arithmetic; retained as optional interpretation |
   339	| D22 `(H-AD-edge)` | supplies `W_±`, separated bulk packets, and `Q_tot=Q_edge+Q_bulk` on each channel | no channel object; directly measure D20's local `Q_L^∂` twice | removed completely from `SPT-M'` |
   340	| charge conservation | rearranges the channel equality into `ΔQ_edge=-(Q_bulk,out-Q_bulk,in)` | not needed for same-coset subtraction; D10 conservation only gives the optional current reading in ⟨1⟩5 | removed from quantization; optional for transport semantics |
   341	| definite bulk and edge channel charges | lets the current proof subtract channel eigenvalues | the projective measurements themselves return `q_-` and `q_+`; their common finite-window offset cancels | removed completely |
   342	
   343	The TPM theorem adds three explicit items absent from the current statement:
   344	D26(INT) for the physical on-site circle charge, the two-measurement protocol
   345	(E.4), and the local-relaxation clauses `(E-LR2)--(E-LR3)` (with the common
   346	sequence supplied by **LR1-GEN**).  These are measurement/limit hypotheses,
   347	not disguised scattering hypotheses.
   348	
   349	This is an improvement in **channel independence**, but no unproved logical
   350	implication `(H-AD-edge)⇒(E-LR)` or `(E-LR)⇒(H-AD-edge)` is asserted.  The new
   351	conclusion also has a different honest scope:
   352	
   353	| current conclusion | channel-free TPM conclusion |
   354	|---|---|
   355	| per-channel operator bookkeeping (6.1) | operational two-readout history law and its dephased first-moment ledger (E.8) |
   356	| integral fixed-system channel differences | every measured memory outcome is in `ℤ` |
   357	| AKLT edge-doublet support contained in `{-1,0,+1}` after restricting the channel edge multiplet | support contained in `ℤ`; no finite support bound without an additional edge-subspace confinement hypothesis |
   358	| expectations are convex combinations and need not be integers | `Σ_mmr(m)` is an arbitrary probability average and need not be an integer |
   359	| topology protects module/capacity, not amplitude | unchanged |
   360	
