   908	# The universality class of the soft factor — D24
   909	
   910	*Promoted at the 2026-08-26 freeze from `theory/ml5-universality.md`
   911	⟨1⟩1--⟨1⟩3 and repaired after the r1 verdict.  D24 fixes the source class;
   912	ML5-A/B were promoted per corpus-r2 while microscopic membership remains open.
   913	Outside the class, unrestricted
   914	universality is refuted by the explicit counterexample in (e).*
   915	
   916	## D24 (hard sources, the contact first jet, and the no-contact class `𝒮_W`)
   917	
   918	**(a) Source class.**  A *local source* is an element of `𝔄_loc`.  An
   919	*exponentially quasi-local source* is a norm-convergent sum `O = Σ_X O_X` with
   920	`‖O‖_μ := Σ_X e^{μ\,diam(X)}‖O_X‖ < ∞` for some `μ > 0`.  Local sources have
   921	finite `‖·‖_μ`.
   922	
   923	**(b) Amputated amplitudes, and the normalisation they are measured in.**
   924	For a source `O`, `M_1^O(h)` is its amputated one-hard amplitude and
   925	`M_2^O(k,h)` its connected hard-plus-soft amplitude in the physical channel;
   926	both are linear in `O`, and both are measured as multipliers in `L²(I,dh)`
   927	for a fixed hard window `I = [a,b] ⋐ (0,π)`.  Remainders are measured in
   928	`‖R_{S2}(k)‖_{L²(I)} ≤ C_I|k|²‖M_1^O‖_{L²(I)}`, or, for
   929	`f_ε(k) = ε^{-1/2}f(k/ε)`, as `O(ε²)` in the product packet norm.  Plane
   930	waves are generalised kernels inside `C_c^∞` packets (D3(a), D12(a′)).

===== current SPT proof relevant =====
