   750	M-quant is conditional on its asymptotic decomposition.  Given (H-split),
   751	(H-AD-edge), charge conservation, and definite channel charges, SPT-M' is
   752	PROVED as this conditional implication.  It uses only the fixed-tensor
   753	congruence in SPT-E'(iii), not deformation constancy.  □
   754	
   755	### ⟨2⟩2. What “protected edge magnon memory” can honestly mean
   756	
   757	**Protection scope (not a nonzero-amplitude conclusion):** a nontrivial `[ω]`
   758	protects the existence of a projective edge module and hence a memory
   759	*capacity* of dimension at least `d_ω`; symmetric local edge terms cannot
   760	replace it by a unique symmetric state.  **Justification:** SPT-E'(ii);
   761	Schur's lemma.
   762	
   763	**CONJECTURE SPT-M'-dyn:** for the specific D23/(2.5a) open AKLT parent
   764	Hamiltonian `H_{A,+}^{dyn}` with boundary coupling
   765	`h_{mag-edge}=P^{(S=2)}_{0,1}`, at least one symmetry-allowed edge-changing
   766	reflection matrix element is nonzero on an open momentum interval, and the
   767	post-selected memory obeys (6.1).  The exact missing step is a half-chain
   768	scattering calculation establishing (H-AD-edge), the on-shell reflection
   769	matrix, and nonvanishing of that matrix element.
   770	
   771	The following statements are **not** claimed:
   772	
   773	* nonzero edge-changing reflection at every momentum;
   774	* vanishing memory for every trivial boundary (accidental trivial edge modes
   775	  can store memory);
   776	* quantisation of an unconditioned expectation value;
   777	* permanence without an isolated charge-preserving edge after the packet has
   778	  departed.
   779	
   780	This is the precise S6-safe boundary between topological protection and
   781	model-dependent dynamics.
