   317	*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩4--⟨1⟩5 and D1(a).
   318	
   319	**⟨2⟩2.**  By Stone's theorem there is a self-adjoint `Q̂` with
   320	`U(θ)=e^{iθQ̂}`.
   321	
   322	*Justification.*  Strong continuity and the group law from ⟨2⟩1; exact
   323	functional-analytic fact **FOL-STONE.1** on the D1(a) GNS Hilbert space.
   324	
   325	**⟨2⟩3.**  `γ_{2π}=id_𝔄`; hence `U(2π)∈π(𝔄)'=ℂ𝟙`, so for some real `q_0`,
   326	
   327	`e^{2πiQ̂}=U(2π)=e^{2πiq_0}𝟙`.
   328	
   329	*Justification.*  D26 gives `e^{2πiS^z}=c𝟙` on each site, whose adjoint
   330	action is the identity on every local algebra and hence on `𝔄` by D1(a).
   331	Then use ⟨1⟩3 and ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2.  Named calculation **FOL-PER.1**.
   332	
   333	**⟨2⟩4.**  The spectral measure of `Q̂` is supported on
   334	`{λ:e^{2πiλ}=e^{2πiq_0}}=q_0+ℤ`.  Therefore
   335	
   336	`𝟙=Σ_{n∈ℤ}E_{Q̂}({q_0+n})`
   337	
   338	strongly, so `Q̂` is pure point and `spec Q̂⊆q_0+ℤ`.
   339	
   340	*Justification.*  Spectral functional calculus applied to ⟨2⟩3; this is the
   341	same arithmetic implication as `theory/memory-index.md` ⟨1⟩2 and is named
   342	here **FOL-SPEC.1** (with D26 supplying the scalar-period premise).
   343	
   344	**⟨2⟩5. QED.**
