   171	`n→-∞` D14 assigns its separated number to the reflected/left leg.
   172	
   173	*Justification.*  D14 and spin `1/2` in D16.
   174	
   175	**⟨2⟩3. QED.**
   176	
   177	**⟨1⟩2. PROVE.**  For `n≥0`, `R_n` is one up hole at site
   178	`y=μ+n+1≥m` on the `↓` vacuum, together with the outgoing kink at bond
   179	`μ-1=m-2`.
   180	
   181	**⟨2⟩1.**  The walls `(μ-1,y-1,y)` enclose exactly the single up spin `y`
   182	after the first `↑↓` wall at `μ-1`.
   183	
   184	*Justification.*  The §5 formula for `R_n` and the D16 vacua.
   185	
   186	**⟨2⟩2.**  Its leg charge relative to the `↓` vacuum is `+1`, and as
   187	`n→+∞` D14 assigns its separated number to the transmitted/right leg.
   188	
   189	*Justification.*  D14 and spin `1/2` in D16.
   190	
   191	**⟨2⟩3. QED.**
   192	
   193	**⟨1⟩3. PROVE.**  Both tails and the side state lie in the same regularised
   194	charge sector.
   195	
   196	**⟨2⟩1.**  Relative to a fixed cut `c`, the negative tail has total charge
   197	`(μ+1-c)-1=μ-c`.
   198	
   199	*Justification.*  D13(a)'s sharp-kink charge and the D14 charge `-1` from
   200	⟨1⟩1.
   201	
   202	**⟨2⟩2.**  The positive tail has total charge
   203	`(μ-1-c)+1=μ-c`, while `K_μ` has charge `μ-c`.
   204	
   205	*Justification.*  D13(a), D14, and ⟨1⟩2.
   206	
   207	**⟨2⟩3.**  Thus transmission changes the kink bond by exactly `-2` while
