   243	**⟨2⟩3. QED.**
   244	
   245	**⟨1⟩2. PROVE.**  A three-wall vertex `(a,b,c)` has a nonzero compressed
   246	hopping edge exactly when `b=a+1` or `c=b+1`.
   247	
   248	**⟨2⟩1.**  By ⟨1⟩1, exchanging at one of `a,b,c` retains at most three walls
   249	only if at least one of its neighbouring bonds is already a wall; otherwise
