   313	## 5. Explicit finite-volume unitary and Hamiltonian
   314	
   315	Put `I_{A,B}={A+1-μ,…,B-μ-2}`.  For `n≤0` and `n≥0`, respectively, let the
   316	following symbols denote the already-enumerated product words:
   317	
   318	`w(L_n)=(μ+n-1,μ+n,μ+1)`,
   319	
   320	`w(R_n)=(μ-1,μ+n,μ+n+1)`.
   321	
   322	The two formulas agree at `n=0`; call that common word `J_0`.  Define on the
   323	orthonormal product basis of `C_{A,B}`
   324	
   325	\[
   326	 U_{A,B}L_n=|n\rangle\quad(n\le0),\qquad
   327	 U_{A,B}R_n=|n\rangle\quad(n\ge0),\qquad
   328	 U_{A,B}K_\mu=|d\rangle .                                      \tag{E.1}
   329	\]
   330	
   331	Only labels with `n∈I_{A,B}` occur.
   332	
   333	**⟨1⟩1. PROVE.**  Equation (E.1) extends uniquely to a unitary
   334	`C_{A,B}→ℓ²(I_{A,B})⊕ℂ|d⟩`.
   335	
   336	**⟨2⟩1.**  The negative labels enumerate the row, the positive labels
   337	enumerate the column, `n=0` is their unique intersection, and `d` is the
   338	unique one-wall state.
   339	
   340	*Justification.*  §4 ⟨1⟩3--⟨1⟩5 and D16.
   341	
   342	**⟨2⟩2.**  Distinct D16 `S^z` product words are orthonormal, and the graph
   343	vectors on the right of (E.1) are an orthonormal basis of the target.
   344	
   345	*Justification.*  D16 and §4 ⟨1⟩5.
   346	
   347	**⟨2⟩3. QED.**
   348	
   349	**⟨1⟩2. PROVE.**  With missing neighbours at the ends of `I_{A,B}` omitted,
   350	
   351	\[
   352	 U_{A,B}H_3U_{A,B}^*|n\rangle
   353	 ={3J\Delta\over2}|n\rangle-{J\over2}(|n-1\rangle+|n+1\rangle)
   354	 -{J\over2}\mathbf1_{n=0}|d\rangle,                            \tag{E.2}
   355	\]
   356	
   357	\[
   358	 U_{A,B}H_3U_{A,B}^*|d\rangle
   359	 ={J\Delta\over2}|d\rangle-{J\over2}|0\rangle .              \tag{E.3}
   360	\]
   361	
   362	**⟨2⟩1.**  In D16, each antiparallel bond contributes diagonal energy
   363	`JΔ/2`, so every path vertex has energy `3JΔ/2` and `K_μ` has energy
   364	`JΔ/2`.
   365	
   366	*Justification.*  Direct two-site matrix of the D16 bond term.
   367	
   368	**⟨2⟩2.**  Every surviving exchange in §2 has matrix element `-J/2`, and
   369	there are no other compressed edges.
   370	
   371	*Justification.*  The D16 XY coefficient and §4 ⟨1⟩4--⟨1⟩5.
   372	
   373	**⟨2⟩3.**  Applying the basis unitary (E.1) gives (E.2)--(E.3).
   374	
   375	*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩1, ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2, and D16.
   376	
   377	**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
   378	
   379	**⟨1⟩3.**  Equations (E.2)--(E.3) are the finite-interval compression of
   380	(Mq.7): a uniform Jacobi path with on-site energy `E_c=3JΔ/2`, hopping
   381	`-J/2`, and a side level `E_d=JΔ/2` coupled at `0` by `-J/2`.
   382	
   383	*Justification.*  Claim Mq-AD3, equation (Mq.7), and ⟨1⟩2.
   384	
   385	**⟨1⟩4. QED.**
