   387	## 6. Exact local-observable map
   388	
   389	Fix a finite site window `W` and `O∈𝔄_W`.  Write `P_C` for the projection
   390	onto `C_∞`.  Let `K_{μ+1}` and `K_{μ-1}` be the sharp D16 kink words on the
   391	left and right channel backgrounds, and put
   392	
   393	`o_L(O)=⟨K_{μ+1}|O|K_{μ+1}⟩`,
   394	`o_R(O)=⟨K_{μ-1}|O|K_{μ-1}⟩`.
   395	
   396	These are evaluations of the already-fixed D16 product vacua/kinks, not new
   397	memory observables.
   398	
   399	**⟨1⟩1. PROVE.**  There is a finite graph set `S_W⊂ℤ∪{d}` such that
   400	
   401	\[
   402	 U_\infty P_CO P_CU_\infty^*
   403	 =o_L(O)\Pi^-_W+o_R(O)\Pi^+_W+F_W,                              \tag{E.4}
   404	\]
   405	
   406	where `Π^-_W` and `Π^+_W` project onto sufficiently remote negative and
   407	positive tails, respectively, and `F_W=P_{S_W}F_WP_{S_W}`.
   408	
   409	**⟨2⟩1.**  For all sufficiently negative `n`, the moving down spin of `L_n`
   410	lies outside `W`, and the restriction of `L_n` to `W` equals that of
   411	`K_{μ+1}`.  For all sufficiently positive `n`, the moving up spin of `R_n`
   412	lies outside `W`, and its restriction equals that of `K_{μ-1}`.
   413	
   414	*Justification.*  The explicit leg coordinates in §3 and the D16 product
   415	basis.
   416	
   417	**⟨2⟩2.**  A `W`-local operator has zero matrix element between two product
   418	words that differ at any site outside `W`.  Hence each sufficiently remote
   419	tail row and column is diagonal, with diagonal value `o_L(O)` or `o_R(O)`.
   420	
   421	*Justification.*  Local tensor-product action in the D16 product basis.
   422	
   423	**⟨2⟩3.**  Only finitely many graph words have their moving spin in `W`; add
   424	those labels, the junction neighbourhood, and `d` to `S_W`.  Subtracting the
   425	two remote diagonal constants then leaves a matrix supported on `S_W`.
   426	
   427	*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2; the exhaustive product-word locality falsifier
   428	is `check_mq_e.py`, with recorded green/red result in `CHECK_OUTPUT.md`.
   429	
   430	**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
   431	
   432	**⟨1⟩2. PROVE.**  Equation (E.4) supplies the local-observable statement
   433	needed for D18(AD3).
   434	
   435	**⟨2⟩1.**  The two tail constants are precisely the local expectations of
   436	the remaining left/right kink charge eigenstates; after subtracting the
   437	appropriate channel constant, the graph observable is `F_W`, which has
   438	finite support.
   439	
   440	*Justification.*  D18(AD3) and ⟨1⟩1.
   441	
   442	**⟨2⟩2.**  Jacobi local decay therefore removes the free leg and non-bound
   443	dressing from every fixed window without discarding coherent reflected/
   444	transmitted superpositions.
   445	
   446	*Justification.*  Claim Mq-AD3 and the finite-support remainder in ⟨2⟩1.
   447	
   448	**⟨2⟩3. QED.**
   449	
   450	**⟨1⟩3. PROVE.**  For a window containing the three kink bonds and with the
   451	separated leg outside it, D13(a)'s wall observable has tail values
   452	`o_L(𝔛_W)=μ+1`, `o_R(𝔛_W)=μ-1`, and side value
   453	`⟨K_μ|𝔛_W|K_μ⟩=μ`.
   454	
   455	**⟨2⟩1.**  D13(a) equals the wall bond on every sharp kink with no other
   456	content in the window.
   457	
   458	*Justification.*  D13(a).
   459	
   460	**⟨2⟩2.**  The channel kink bonds and side bond are those established in §3.
   461	
   462	*Justification.*  §3 ⟨1⟩1--⟨1⟩3, D14, and D16.
   463	
   464	**⟨2⟩3.**  Thus the local-observable map records exactly zero reflected
   465	displacement and transmitted displacement `-2`.
   466	
   467	*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2, D13(a), and D14.
   468	
   469	**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
   470	
   471	**⟨1⟩4.**  The literal statement “every fixed-window observable maps to a
   472	finite-support graph observable” must be read with channel-kink subtraction:
   473	without subtraction, the exact mapping is the two-constant formula (E.4).
   474	
   475	*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩1--⟨1⟩3 and D18(AD3).
   476	
   477	**⟨1⟩5. QED.**
   478	
   479	## 7. Claim closure
   480	
   481	**⟨1⟩1. PROVE.**  Mq-E holds with all data required in its claim row.
   482	
   483	**⟨2⟩1.**  Enumeration/component, finite unitary, infinite compatibility,
   484	labels/charges, and observables are proved in §§1--6, respectively.
   485	
   486	*Justification.*  §§1--6 and D14--D16.  **⟨2⟩2. QED.**
   487	
   488	**⟨1⟩2. PROVE.**  On the projected incoming component, M-tk is unconditional:
   489	`t(k)=[1+iJ²/(4ω(k)v(k))]^{-1}` and
   490	`T(k)=16(Δ-1)²k²+O(k⁴)`.
   491	
   492	**⟨2⟩1.**  M-tk and Mq-AD3 prove these consequences conditional only on the
   493	Mq-E premise, which ⟨1⟩1 discharges.
   494	
   495	*Justification.*  D15--D16 and claims M-tk, Mq-AD3.  The claim scope leaves
   496	the unprojected formula and universality open.  **⟨2⟩2. QED.**
   497	
   498	**⟨1⟩3. QED.** □

