   697	## D18 (hypothesis (H-AD): wave operators, channels, and local decay)
   698	
   699	Fix a conserved regularised-charge sector of a finite-range `U(1)`-invariant
   700	dynamics, free left/right one-particle channel spaces `ℋ_L,ℋ_R`,
   701	`ℋ_as := ℋ_L ⊕ ℋ_R`, channel Hamiltonian `H_as`, an identification `J`, and
   702	channel projections `P_L,P_T`.  The sector satisfies **(H-AD)** for a selected
   703	one-kink/one-magnon scattering vector iff all four clauses below hold.
   704	
   705	**(AD1: wave operators and completeness.)**  The strong limits
   706	
   707	  `W_± := s-lim_{t→±∞} e^{itH}J e^{-itH_as}`
   708	
   709	exist as isometries with common range `ℋ_sc`, and the physical sector has the
   710	orthogonal decomposition `ℋ = ℋ_b ⊕ ℋ_sc`, where `ℋ_b` contains spatially
   711	localised bound states.  There is no further propagating channel.
   712	
   713	**(AD2: selected scattering vector.)**  The vector is `Ψ = W_-(φ,0)`,
   714	`φ ∈ ℋ_L`, has no `ℋ_b` component, and
   715	`W_+^*Ψ = (φ_R,φ_T)`.  On `ℋ_sc` define
   716	
   717	  `N_T := W_+P_TW_+^*`,  `⟨N_T⟩ := ‖φ_T‖²`.
   718	
   719	For an on-shell diagonal scattering matrix,
   720	`⟨N_T⟩ = ∫(dk/2π)|φ(k)|²T(k)`; it is a packet average, not generally `T` at
   721	the mean momentum.
   722	
   723	**(AD3: channel charges and local decay.)**  The incoming left leg has charge
   724	`q_in` relative to the left vacuum and each outgoing leg has a stated charge
   725	`q_out` relative to its vacuum.  For every fixed window containing the kink,
   726	the free leg charge and non-bound dressing leave the window as `t→±∞`; the
   727	remaining local state is a kink charge eigenstate, and the increasing-window
   728	limit of D13(a) exists on it.
   729	
   730	**(AD4: order of limits.)**  Infinite-volume dynamics and the wave operators
   731	are formed before `t→±∞`; fixed-window scattering limits are formed before
   732	the window is increased to `ℤ`.
   733	
   734	H-AD is narrower than general many-body asymptotic completeness and is an
   735	explicit hypothesis unless a separate theorem supplies AD1--AD4.  It is a
   736	coherent Hilbert-space statement: reflected/transmitted superpositions are
   737	retained, not replaced in norm by classical mixtures.
   738	
   739	**Superseded r1 formulation.**  The former D18 required the in/out state to be
   740	norm-close to a convex mixture of product configurations.  That condition is
   741	withdrawn.  For `|ψ_out⟩ = r|R⟩+t|T⟩` with `rt ≠ 0` and orthogonal separated
   742	channels, the pure density matrix retains the cross terms
   743	`r\bar t|R⟩⟨T| + \bar r t|T⟩⟨R|`; its norm distance from the diagonal mixture
   744	does not vanish.  AD3 uses local decay without discarding this coherence.
