    64	| SPT-M'-dyn | None | Half-chain wave operators, an on-shell reflection matrix, and nonvanishing remain open. | **Not supplied by phase classification.** |
    65	| SPT-B-mult / SPT-B' | Whole-chain genuine action and phase stability | Left/right projective multipliers cancel in the whole-chain action, while the individual half-chain class survives.  Stability of the class does not quantise arbitrary bulk coefficients. | **Consistent, not equivalent.** |
    66	| A-INDEX-TC-fin / A-INDEX-PEPS | Higher-dimensional endpoint/anyon selection, not the 1D split index | These rows concern 2D annular/ribbon or categorical registers. | **Outside the 1D Ogata comparison.** |
    67	
    68	**Literature premise for the Ogata-side column:** OGA-SURVEY and OGA-LSM,
    69	both **UNVERIFIED-NEEDS-FETCH** as listed in section 2.  **Local
    70	justification:** D26--D27; claims M-INDEX-fin, M-INDEX-spec,
    71	M-INDEX-LA-folium, M-INDEX-LA-strong, M-IDX-density, SPT-B-mult, SPT-B',
    72	SPT-E', SPT-T', SPT-D', SPT-M', SPT-M'-dyn, A-INDEX-TC-fin and
    73	A-INDEX-PEPS.
    74	
    75	## 4. The implementer map, without conflating the objects
    76	
    77	The map has four levels.  Only the middle two are Ogata/SPT objects.
    78	
    79	| level | object | what its `2pi` information means |
    80	|---|---|---|
    81	| microscopic site | D26's `exp(2pi i S^z_x)=c I` | All one-site charge eigenvalues lie in one coset `kappa+Z`.  The scalar disappears in the adjoint action. |
    82	| whole-chain GNS | A spatial implementer of the selected circle, if it exists in the chosen folium | In an irreducible representation its `2pi` unitary is scalar, so its Stone generator has spectrum in one integer coset.  This is the implementer route of M-INDEX-LA-folium. |
    83	| split half-chain | Ogata's right implementer `u_R(g)` | It is projective; its multiplier gives the `H^2` SPT class.  The left implementer carries the inverse multiplier so the whole-chain action is genuine.  **UNVERIFIED-NEEDS-FETCH arXiv:2110.04671, arXiv:1810.01045.** |
    84	| MPS edge register | D21/SPT-E' `V_C(g)` and `Q_edge=-iX_C^circ` | Under H-split this is the finite-dimensional representative of the preceding half-chain action.  Restricting the full projective action to the selected circle gives the shifted edge weights, subject to D21's full-group normalization. |
    85	
    86	Thus the proposed identification is
    87	
    88	`Ogata u_R(g)` --(MPS/split intertwiner)--> `V_C(g)`
    89	`                                  ` --(circle derivative and centering)--> `Q_edge`,
    90	
    91	not `Ogata u_R(g) = exp(i theta Qhat_{W,c_0})`.  The latter is a local
    92	finite-window observable and need not converge to any total-charge operator;
    93	claim M-INDEX-LA-strong is already REFUTED.
    94	
    95	The type of the half-chain factor is a gate, not extra topological data.  In
    96	the split SPT construction it is type I by definition/the unique-gapped-state
    97	input (**UNVERIFIED-NEEDS-FETCH arXiv:2110.04671**).  A genuinely type-III
    98	half-chain factor is therefore outside that split construction and cannot be
    99	used to discharge H-split.  M-INDEX-fin remains valid there because it never
   100	uses a half-chain factor.  OGA-TYPEIII concerns general type-III factor
   101	flexibility, not an alternative derivation of the 1D split SPT index.
   102	
